            comment Comment15 START <!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC "-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.0//EN" "http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40/strict.dtd"><html><head><meta name="qrichtext" content="1" /><meta charset="utf-8" /><style type="text/css">p, li { white-space: pre-wrap; }hr { height: 1px; border-width: 0; }li.unchecked::marker { content: "\2610"; }li.checked::marker { content: "\2612"; }</style></head><body style=" font-family:'Sans'; font-size:12pt; font-weight:400; font-style:normal;"><p style=" margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;"><span style=" font-family:'Segoe UI'; font-size:16pt;">The inputs are set to </span><span style=" font-family:'Segoe UI'; font-size:16pt; font-weight:700;">ex_rate</span><span style=" font-family:'Segoe UI'; font-size:16pt;">, <br />while the internal calculations, outputs, and measurements <br />are set to </span><span style=" font-family:'Segoe UI'; font-size:16pt; font-weight:700;">Ts</span><span style=" font-family:'Segoe UI'; font-size:16pt;">. This allows higher accuracy <br />in parts of the model that require a smaller execution step, <br />while reducing overall CPU usage.</span></p></body></html> ENDCOMMENT 
